hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2311","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Abdullah bin Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The example of a miserly person and a charitable person is like two men wearing iron robes whose hands are forced to Between them, the more the charitable person intends to give charity, the more it expands until his effect is relieved, and the more the miserly person intends to give charity, the more each episode becomes limited until She accompanied her, squeezed him close to him, and his hands joined his collarbones, and I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He will strive to He expands it, but it does not expand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2312","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Khaled, he is Ibn Yazid, told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hilal, on the authority of Umayyah ibn Hind, on the authority of Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hanif, who said: One day we were sitting in the mosque, and a group of people The Muhajireen and the Ansar. So we sent a man to Aisha to ask permission, so we entered upon her. She said: A beggar entered upon me once, and with me is a messenger. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so I ordered something for him, then I called for him and looked at him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do you not want to Nothing enters your house or leaves except with your knowledge. I said: Yes. He said: Wait, Aisha, do not count, and God will count for you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2313","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “No “You count, and God counts you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2314","I am Al-Hasan bin Muhammad, on the authority of Hajjaj, Ibn Jurayj said: Ibn Abi Mulaika told me, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Asma bint Abu Bakr, she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, I have nothing to do except what Al-Zubayr has entered upon me. Do I have any right to submit to what comes upon me? He said: “Be submissive as much as you can, and do not despair, for God will help you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2315","Nasr bin Ali reported, on the authority of Khalid ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu`bah reported, on the authority of Al-Muhall bin Khalifa, Thiqah Kufi, on the authority of Uday Ibn Hatim, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fear Hell, even if it is half a date.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2316","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, that Amr bin Murrah told them, on the authority of Khaythamah, On the authority of Adi bin Hatim, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned Hell, so he turned his face away and sought refuge from it. Shu’bah mentioned that He did that three times, then said: “Fear the Fire, even if it is half a date, and if you do not find it, then with a kind word.”"
"2317","Azhar bin Jamil told us, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, and he mentioned Aoun bin Abi Juhayfah, he said: I heard Al-Mundhir bin Jarir, on the authority of his father, said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the dawn of the day, when a naked, barefoot people came Swords caused harm to most of them, nay, all of them caused harm. The face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, changed when he saw the poverty in them, so he entered. Then he went out and ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer, then he established the prayer and prayed, then he delivered a sermon and said: O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a soul. And from her He created its mate and spread from them many men and women, and fear God, by whom you ask, and the relatives. Indeed, God is a watcher over you. Fear God, and let a soul see what it has put forward for tomorrow. A man gives in charity from his dinar, from his dirham, from his garment, from a saa of his righteousness, from a saa of his dates, Until he said: “Even if it were half a date.” Then a man from the Ansar came with a basket that his hand was almost unable to handle, in fact it was unable to handle. Then the people continued until I saw two piles of food and clothes, until I saw the face of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shining as if it were golden, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever establishes a good practice in Islam will have its reward and the reward of whoever acts according to it without it detracting from their wages in the slightest. And whoever establishes In Islam there is a bad Sunnah, so he bears its burden and the burden of whoever acts according to it without it diminishing anything from their burdens.”"
"2318","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ma`bad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Haritha, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give alms, for a time will come upon you when a man will walk away with his charity and the one who gave it will say: If only You brought it yesterday and accepted it, but today you did not.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2319","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Burda bin Abdullah bin Abi Burda told me, On the authority of his grandfather, Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Intercede, intercede, and God will judge what is \"He willed\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2320","Harun bin Saeed Al-Aili reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Munabbih, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man will ask me for something, so I will withhold it until you intercede on it and you will be rewarded.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Intercede and you will be rewarded.”"
"2321","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Kawsaj reported, he said: Muhammad bin Yusuf reported, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, He said: Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith Al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Ibn Jabir, on the authority of his father, and he is Jabir bin Atik, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God Almighty bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, among jealousy is that which loves God Almighty, and among it is that which hates God Almighty, and among it is vanity that which loves God Almighty.” And among them is that which God Almighty and Majestic hates. As for the jealousy that God Almighty loves, it is jealousy due to suspicion, and as for the jealousy that He hates God Almighty, for jealousy is without suspicion, and the arrogance that God Almighty loves is a man’s pride in himself when fighting and when Charity, and the arrogance that God Almighty hates: arrogance in falsehood.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2322","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammam reported, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat, give in charity, and dress without extravagance or imagination.”"
"2323","Abdullah bin Al-Haytham bin Othman told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A believer to another believer is like a building supported by its parts.” \"some\""
"2324","He said: “The trustworthy treasurer who gives what he is ordered to do, willingly with it himself, is one of the charitable people.”"
"2325","Muhammad bin Salamah reported to Abu al-Harith al-Masry, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who recites the Qur’an loudly is like one who recites the Qur’an openly.” “With charity, and one who is pleased with the Qur’an is like one who is pleased with charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2326","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Omar bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three whom God will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: The one who is disobedient to his parents.” A promiscuous woman, a cuckold, and three will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the one who is addicted to alcohol, and the one who is ungrateful with what he gives. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2327","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mudrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, on the authority of Kharshah bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three whom God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them.” “And He will not purify them, and they will have a painful punishment.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it, and Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. They were disappointed and lost. He said: “The one who sends his garment is arrogance, the one who spends his goods is his false oath, and the one who is generous is his giving.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2328","Bishr ibn Khalid reported, he said: Ghandar reported, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I heard Suleiman, who is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Mushar, On the authority of Kharshah ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor He will look down upon them, but will not purify them, and for them is a painful punishment: the one who is generous with what he has given, the one who gives away his sins, and the one who spends his goods by a false oath.”"
"2329","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, and Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Bujayd Al-Ansari, on the authority of his grandmother, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Refuse the questioner, even if it is with an unjust tone.” In the hadith of Aaron: “burnt”"
"2330","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, he said: Mu`tamar narrated to us, he said: I heard Bahz ibn Hakim narrating, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A man who is his master does not come and ask him of a bounty that he has and he withholds it from him, unless he will be called for it on the Day of The Resurrection is a brave and humble man who relishes the bounty that was withheld.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2331","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “Whoever seeks refuge in God, grant him protection; whoever asks you in God, give him; whoever seeks refuge in God, grant him protection; whoever comes to you “And if you do not find it, then pray for him until you know that you have repaid him.”"
"2332","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala reported, he said: Mu`tamar told us, he said: I heard Bahz ibn Hakim speaking, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I said: O Prophet of God, I had not come to you before I had sworn by more people than the number of the fingers of his hands that I would not come to you or your religion, and that I was a man who did not understand anything except What have God and His Messenger taught me, and I ask you in the face of God about what your Lord has sent you to us? He said: “By Islam.” He said: I said: What are the signs of Islam? He said: “That you should say: I have surrendered my face to God and renounced myself, and establish prayer and pay zakat. Every Muslim over a mahram Muslim is two helping brothers, no.” “God will accept a deed from a polytheist after he has submitted to Islam, or He will separate from the polytheists for Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2333","Muhammad bin Rafi’ narrated, saying: Ibn Abi Fudaik narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated, on the authority of Sa’id bin Khalid Al-Qarizi, On the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Doesn’t Shall I inform you of the best of people in status? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: A man who takes the head of his horse in the cause of God until he dies or is killed. Shall I inform you of the one that comes next? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: A man who isolates himself among a people who performs prayer, pays zakat, and avoids evil. People, and should I inform you about the worst of people? We said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “The one who asks by God and does not give by Him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2334","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I heard Ruba’i narrated, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Dhabyan, who transmitted it to Abu Dharr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There are three whom God loves, and three whom God hates. Those whom God loves: A man came to a people and asked them about God, but he did not ask them because he was related to them, so they prevented him, so a man left him behind. after them, so he gave him a secret. No one knows about his gift except God Almighty and the One who gave him. And there are people who walked throughout the night even when they were asleep. dearer to them than anything that is equal to them. They descended and lowered their heads, and he stood up to flatter Me and recite My verses, and a man who was in a company met the enemy and was defeated. So he approached his chest until he was killed or God granted him victory. And the three whom God hates: the adulterous old man, the deceitful poor man, and the rich man. “The oppressors” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2335","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail narrated, he said: Sharik narrated, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “It is not the poor person who is rejected by one date and two dates, and a morsel and two morsels. Rather, it is the poor person who is chaste. Recite: Whatever you wish: They do not ask people forcefully.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This partner is Ibn Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, who is not strong in Hadith"
"2336","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “The poor person is not like this tawaf that goes around people and is returned to him by one bite and two bites, and one date and two dates.” They said: What is the poor person? He said: “He who does not find wealth to enrich it, and does not understand what he has and does not give him alms, and does not stand up and ask people.”"
"2337","Nasr bin Ali reported, he said: Abd al-Ala reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not the poor person whom one eater and two eaters reject, and one date and two dates.” They said: So what Poor person, O Messenger of God? He said: “The one who is not rich, and the people do not know his need, so he should be given alms.”"
"2338","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bujaid, on the authority of his grandmother, Umm Bujaid. She was among those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The poor man should stand at my door.” I cannot find anything for him to give him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “If you do not find anything, then you can give him anything except a burnt hoove.” So give it to him.”"
"2339","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “There are three whom God will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection: the adulterous sheikh, the proud breadwinner, and the false imam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2340","Abu Dawud narrated, he said: A`rim narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There are four whom God Almighty hates: the unjust seller, the deceitful poor, And the adulterous sheikh, and the unjust imam.”"
"2341","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Thawr bin Zayd al-Dili, on the authority of Abu Al-Ghaith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who takes care of the widow and the poor is like the one who strives in the cause of God.”"
"2342","Hannad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: While he was in Yemen, Ali sent gold with its soil to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, distributed it. May God bless him and grant him peace, among four people: Al-Aqra’ bin Habis Al-Hanathili, Uyaynah bin Badr Al-Fazari, Alqamah bin Ulatha Al-Amiri, then “One of the Banu Kilab, Zayd al-Tai, then one of the Banu Nabhan.” The Quraysh became angry and said: “Once again, the Quraysh’s boxes.” They said: “You give the Quraysh’s boxes.” We will come and let us go. He said: “I only did that to get along with them.” Then a man with a thick beard, with high cheeks and sunken eyes, came. He raised his forehead and shaved his head and said: Fear God, O Muhammad. He said: Who will obey God Almighty if I disobey Him? Will he trust me with the people of the earth? And you do not trust me? Then the man turned around, and a man from the people asked permission to kill him. They believed that he was Khalid bin Al-Walid, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “No, from among this light are people who recite the Qur’an but it does not go beyond their throats. They kill the people of Islam and call on the people of Islam.” Idols, they pass away from Islam as an arrow passes from the target. If I overtake them, I will kill them with a common killing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2343","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi reported, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Harun bin Riyab, who said: Kinana bin Nu’aym told me. And Ali bin Hajar reported, and the pronunciation of it, he said: Ishmael reported, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Aaron, on the authority of Kinanah ibn Nu’aym, on the authority of Qabisah. Ibn Mukhariq, he said: He said: I carried a burden and came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about it? He said: “The issue is not permissible except for three people: a man who carries a burden among a people and asks for it until he carries it, then he holds back.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2344","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar narrated, saying: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Harun ibn Riyab, he said: Kinanah ibn Nu`aym narrated to me, on the authority of Qubaisah. Ibn Mukhariq, he said: I carried a burden and came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to ask him about it. He said: “Stay, O Qubaysah, until you come to us.” Charity, so we command it for you.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Qubaysah, charity is not permissible except for one of three people: a man.” He carried a burden, and the matter was resolved for him, so that he might gain a means of living, or he said: a means of sustenance, and a man was afflicted with poverty, so that he might bear witness. Three of his people who made the Hajj: A calamity has befallen so-and-so, so the matter has been resolved for him so that he can make a living, or he said: make up for his livelihood. livelihood, and a man was struck by a plague, ravaging his wealth, and the matter was resolved for him until it afflicted it, then he refrained from it. There is nothing else besides this. “The issue, O Qabisah, is an unlawful thing that its owner eats unlawfully.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2345","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail bin Aliyah told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, he said: Hilal told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on the pulpit and we sat. He turned it around and said: “I only fear for you after me what flower will be opened for you, and he mentioned the world and its adornment.” Then a man said: Or will he come? Good with evil? ! The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about him, and it was said to him: What is the matter with you that you speak to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he does not speak to you? He said: We saw that it was descending upon him, so he woke up, wiping the basin, and said: “I bear witness to the questioner, and I did not understand as I wanted. Good does not come with evil. And of the things that bring forth spring, they kill or cause harm, except the one who eats green vegetables, for she eats until, when her sides are extended, she faces the sun’s eyes. Then she urinated, then she urinated, then she urinated, and this money is green and sweet, and what a good companion a Muslim is if he gives it to an orphan. And the poor and the wayfarer, and the one who takes it without his right is like the one who eats and is not satisfied, and he will be a witness against him on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"2346","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm al-Rihih, on the authority of Salman bin Amer, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Charity given to the poor is charity, and it is twofold charity given to a relative: charity and connection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2347","Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari reported. I wrote about him in Basra. He said: Ghandar reported, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zainab, Abdullah’s wife, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to women: “Give alms even if Of your beautiful ones.” She said: Abdullah was light-handed, so she said to him: Can I give my charity to you and to my brother’s children who are orphans? Abdullah said: Ask the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. She said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, at his door was a woman from It is said that the Ansar had Zainab asking about what I was asking about, so Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So ask him about that, and do not tell him who we are. So he went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “Who are they?” He said: Zainab. He said: “Which Zayanab?” He said: Zainab, the wife of Abdullah bin Masoud, and Zainab Al-Ansariyya. He said: “Yes, they have two rewards: the reward of kinship. And the reward of charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2348","Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Ubaid The servant of Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “To be determined.” “One of you buying a bundle of firewood and carrying it on his back and selling it is better than asking a man and him giving it to him or withholding it.”"
"2349","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam reported, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth bin Saad, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Jaafar, who said: I heard Hamza bin Abdullah, saying: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The man continues He will be asked until the Day of Resurrection comes without a speck of flesh on his face.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2350","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi reported, saying: Umayyah ibn Khalid told us, saying: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Bastam ibn Muslim, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Khalifa, on the authority of Aidh bin Amr, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him and he gave him, so when he placed his foot on a roof Chapter, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you knew what was involved in the matter, no one would have gone to anyone and asked him anything.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2351","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Bakr bin Sawadah, on the authority of Muslim bin Makhshi, On the authority of Ibn Al-Farasi, that Al-Farasi said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Shall we ask, O Messenger of God? He said: “No, and if you are asking, you must ask the righteous.”"
"2352","Qutaibah bin Sa’id reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, that people from The Ansar asked the Messenger of God, and he gave them. Then they asked him, and he gave them, until when he ran out of what he had, he said: “Whatever good thing I have.” I will not withhold it from you, and whoever is chaste, God Almighty will pardon him, and whoever is patient, God will grant him patience, and no gift given to anyone is better. And more extensive than patience.”"
"2353","Ali bin Shuaib narrated, he said: Ma’an narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, for one of you to take his rope and collect firewood on his back, it is better for him than A man comes to whom God Almighty has given him out of His bounty, and he asks him whether He gave it to him or withheld it.”"
"2354","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, he said: Muhammad bin Qays told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Thawban, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who can guarantee me one thing and Paradise for him?” Yahya said: Here is a word that means: that people should not ask anything. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2355","Hisham bin Ammar told us: Yahya, who is Ibn Hamza, told us: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Harun bin Ri’ab, that He narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Bakr, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He is Kinanah ibn Nu`aym, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Mukhariq, he said: I heard the Prophet pray May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: “The question is not valid except for three things: A man whose wealth has been struck by an accident, and he asks until he obtains a sufficient amount of livelihood, then He abstains, and a man carries a load among a people, so he asks until he delivers their loads to them, then he abstains from asking, and a man swears three oaths. A group of his people who have the Pilgrimage to God. The matter has been solved for so-and-so, so he asks until he achieves a livelihood, then he refrains from it. The issue, anything else is permissible.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2356","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks will have what It will enrich him if there will be scratches or soreness on his face on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: O Messenger of God, and what will it enrich him or what made him enriched? He said: “Fifty dirhams or its equivalent in gold.” Yahya said: Sufyan said: I heard Zubaid speaking to him, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Yazid. Abu Abdul Rahman said: We do not know of anyone who said in this hadith: Zubaid other than Yahya bin Adam, and we do not know this hadith except from a hadith Hakim bin Jubayr, and Hakim is weak. Shu'bah was asked about the hadith of Hakim, and he said: I fear hell, and it was narrated from him long ago. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2357","Al-Hussein bin Harith reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Wahb bin Munabbih, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Muawiyah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not be ambivalent about the issue, for none of you will ask me anything while I hate it, so I will bless him in what he does.” I gave it to him"
"2358","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Dawud bin Shabour, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib. On the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever asks and has forty dirhams is wearing a veil.”"
"2359","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Ibn Abi Al-Rijal told us, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of His father, he said: My mother sent me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I went to him and sat down, and he greeted me and said: “Whoever is rich, God will make him rich.” And whoever begs, God will pardon him, and whoever is sufficiency, God Almighty will suffice him, and whoever begs and has the value of a waqiya has begged.” So I said: My ruby camel. It is better than an uqiya, so I went back and did not ask him.”"
"2360","He said: Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading it from him, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, On the authority of a man from Banu Asad, who said: My family and I camped in Baqi al-Gharqad, and my family said to me: Go to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he asked him something for us to eat, so I went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and found a man with him asking him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, The Messenger of God, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “I cannot find anything to give you.” Then the man turned away from him in anger, saying to my life, “You can give to whomever you wish.” The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He becomes angry with me if I do not find what to give him. Whoever among you asks and has a uqiyah or is just for it has asked urgently.” Al-Asadi said: So I said: A piece of wheat for us is better than an uqiyah, and an uqiyah is forty dirhams. So I returned and did not ask him, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. After that, he (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) gave us barley and raisins, and he divided some of it for us until God Almighty made us rich."
"2361","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “It is not permissible to give charity to a rich person, nor to a straight person.”"
"2362","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, he said: My father told me, he said: He told me Ubayd Allah ibn Adiy ibn al-Khayyar said that two men told him that they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him for charity, so he turned to them. Sight, and Muhammad said: his sight, and he saw them as two skins, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you wish, I will give you both, and there is no share in it.” “For the rich, nor for the strong, earning one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2363","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who is Ibn Umair, on the authority of Zaid bin Uqba, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Questions are like a toil with which a man scratches his face, so who He may toil himself, and whoever wishes may leave it, unless the man asks a ruler or something for which he can find no alternative.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2364","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan narrated, he said: Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Zayd bin Uqba, On the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “An issue is an issue with which a man will bruise his face, unless the man asks authority, or in a matter that is necessary.”"
"2365","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar Al-Attar Al-Basri reported that he stayed in Mecca, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, who said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, and said: “This money is beautiful and green. Whoever takes it with good will will be blessed for it, and whoever takes it with supervision.” “No soul was blessed for it, and he was like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"
"2366","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Miskin bin Bukayr told us, saying: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, On the authority of Hakim bin Hazzam, he said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O wise man, this money is green and sweet. Whoever takes it generously will be blessed with it. And whoever takes it out of self-control, he will not be blessed for it, and he is like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.”"
"2367","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Jizzi informed us, saying: Ishaq bin Bakr told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, and Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, that Hakim ibn Hazzam said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace So he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then I asked him and he gave me, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Wise One, this is Money is a sweet green thing, so whoever takes it out of generosity, he will be blessed with it, and whoever takes it out of self-indulgence, he will not be blessed with it. Like one who eats and is not satisfied, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand.” A wise man said: So I said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, no I will be superior to anyone after you until I leave this world for a thing."
"2368","Qutaibah bin Sa’id reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Bukayr, on the authority of Bishr bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Al-Sa’idi Al-Maliki, he said: He used me. Omar Ibn Al-Khattab said about the charity, so when I finished it, I gave it to him, so he ordered me to do some work, so I said to him: I only worked for God and my reward is from God. He said: Take what I have given you, for I have worked during the covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said to him: As you said, and the Messenger of God said to me: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If you are given something without asking, then eat and give in charity.”"
"2369","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman Al-Makki reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, on the authority of Huwaytib bin Abd. Al-Uzza said: Abdullah bin Al-Saadi informed me that he came to Omar bin Al-Khattab from the Levant and said: Was I not informed that you are working on a work of The works of Muslims, so you are given work for him and do not accept it? He said: Yes, I have horses and slaves and I am well, and I want my work to be a charity for the Muslims. Omar said: I wanted what you wanted. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give me money, and I would say: Give it to someone who is more in need of it than me. And he once gave me money, so I said to him: Give it to him who is more in need of it than me.” He said: “God has not given you this money without asking or supervising, so take it and finance it or Give it in charity, and if not, do not follow it yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2370","Kathir bin Ubaid Al-Humsi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, that Huwaytib bin Abdul-Uzza told him that Abdullah bin Al-Saadi told him that he came before Omar bin Al-Khattab during his caliphate, so he told him Omar: Didn’t I tell you that you do some of the people’s deeds, so if you are given the deeds, you return them? I said: Yes, and Omar said: What do you want to do with that? So I said: I have horses and slaves, and I am fine, and I want my work to be a charity for the Muslims. So Omar said to him: Do not do it, for I was I wanted something like what you wanted. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give me gifts, and I would say: Give it to someone who is more in need of it than I am. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Take it and finance it or give it in charity. Whatever comes to you of this money and you are neither honorable nor begging, take it, and whatever not, then not.” Your soul will follow it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2371","Amr bin Mansour and Ishaq bin Mansour narrated, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Nafi’, he said: Shuaib narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid told me that Huwaytib bin Abdul-Uzza told him that Abdullah bin Al-Saadi told him that he came to Omar Ibn Al-Khattab in his caliphate, and Omar said: Did I not tell you that you do some of the people’s work, and if you are given work you hate it? He said: I said: Yes, he said: What do you want to do with that? So I said: I have horses and servants, and I am well, and I want my work to be a charity for the Muslims. Omar said: Do not do it, for I was I wanted what I wanted, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give me gifts, and I would say: Give it to him who is more in need of it than me, until he once gave me money, and I said: Give it to someone who is poorer than me. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Take it and finance it and give it in charity. Whatever comes to you of this money while you are not Take him from the honorable and the beggar, but whatever he does not, do not let your soul follow him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2372","Amr bin Mansour narrated, saying: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ narrated to us, saying: Shuaib narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, saying: Salem bin Abd narrated to me. By God, Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard Omar saying: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give me gifts, so I said: Give him whoever he is. He is poorer than me, until he once gave me money, and I said: Give it to someone who is poorer than me, so he said: “Take it and finance it and give it in charity.” If this money comes to you and you are neither honorable nor beggar, then take it, and if not, do not follow it yourself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2373","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad al-Misri informed me, he said: Ibn Wahb informed me, he said: Yunus, who is the son of Yazid, informed me about Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal Al-Hashimi, that Abdul-Muttalib bin Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib He told him that his father, Rabi’ah bin Al-Harith, said to Abdul-Muttalib bin Rabi’ah and Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas: Come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Ali bin Abi Talib came while we were in that state, and he said to them: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not appoint any of you to give charity. Abdul-Muttalib said: So Al-Fadl and I set off until we came to the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “This charity is only the dirt of people, and it is not permissible for Muhammad or the family of Muhammad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2374","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: I said to Abu Iyas Muawiyah ibn Qurrah: Have you heard Anas? Ibn Malik, who says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The nephew of one of the people among them”? He said: Yes"
"2375","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Waki` reported, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The nephew of one of the people.”"
"2376","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rafi’, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed a man from Banu Makhzum to do charity, so Abu Rafi’ wanted to follow him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, charity is not permissible for us, and indeed the people’s friends are among them.”"
"2377","Muhammad ibn Hatim informed us, he said: Hibban informed us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of al-Hakam ibn Utaiba, On the authority of some of his companions, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent Arqam bin Arqam to seek charity, and he said to Abu Rafi’: Could you Will you follow me, and I will give you from the shares of the workers? He said: I will not do what I do until I mention that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he came to him and said: Arqam bin Arqam passed by me and asked Until I catch up with him, and he gives me the share of the workers. Then he said: “O Abu Rafi’, we are the people of a household and it is not permissible for us to give charity, and the people’s master is one of \"themselves\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2378","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Wasil told us, he said: Bahz bin Hakim told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought something, he would ask about it: Is it a gift or charity? If it was said: Charity, he would not eat it, and if it was said: A gift, he extended his hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2379","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, that she wanted to buy Bareerah and free her, and that they made a condition of her loyalty, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “Buy her and free her, for loyalty is to the one who frees her.” She was given the choice when she was freed, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was given. May God bless him and grant him peace, with meat. It was said: This is what she gave in charity to Barira. He said: “It is charity for her and for us a gift.” And her husband was free."
"2380","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Zaid. Ibn Aslam, on the authority of his father, said: I heard Omar saying: I mounted a horse for the sake of God, but the one who had it lost it, so I wanted to He bought it from him, and I thought he was selling it cheaply, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that, and he said: “Do not buy it, even if He gave it to you for a dirham, for the one who returns to his charity is like a dog who returns to his vomit.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2381","Harun bin Ishaq reported, saying: Abdul Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar, that he mounted a horse for the sake of God and saw it being sold, so he wanted to buy it, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do not skimp on your charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2382","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Hujain bin Al-Muthanna told us, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab. On the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, that Abdullah bin Omar used to narrate that Omar bin Al-Khattab gave alms for a horse in the name of God and found it being sold. After that, he wanted to buy it, then he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: May God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not exceed your charity.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2383","Ali bin Hajar narrated to us, he said: Ismail, who is Ibn Jafar, narrated to us, he said: Abu Suhail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Talha bin Ubayd Allah, that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a broken head, and said: O Messenger of God, tell me what God has imposed May the prayers be upon me? He said: “The five daily prayers, unless you do something voluntary.” He said: Tell me what fasting God has made obligatory upon me? He said: “Fasting the month of Ramadan, unless you do something voluntary.” He said: Inform me of what God has obligated me to pay in terms of zakat? So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, informed him of the laws of Islam, and he said: By the One who honored you, I do not volunteer anything, nor do I detract from what God has imposed. I owe something, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He will succeed and his father if he is truthful, or he will enter Paradise and his father if he is truthful.”"
"2384","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, he said: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: We were forbidden in the Qur’an from asking the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about anything, so we were astonished that a sensible man from the people of the desert would come. So he asked him, and a man from the desert came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us and told us that you claim that God sent you. He said: “He spoke the truth.” He said: Who created the sky? He said: “God.” He said: Who created the earth? He said: “God.” He said: Who erected the mountains there? He said: “God.” He said: Who has created benefits in it? He said: “God.” He said: By the One who created the heavens and the earth, and set up the mountains, and placed in them benefits, has God sent you? He said: “Yes.” He said: “And your messenger claimed that we are obligated to perform five prayers every day and night.” He said: “He is right.” He said: “Then by the one who sent you, may God command you.” With this? He said: “Yes.” He said: “And your messenger claimed that we are obligated to give zakat on our wealth.” He said: “He spoke the truth.” He said: “Then by the One who sent you, has God commanded you to do this?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And your messenger claimed that we have to fast the month of Ramadan every year.” He said: “He is right.” He said: “Then by the one who sent you, may God command you.” With this? He said: “Yes.” He said: “And your messenger claimed that Hajj is obligatory for us whoever is able to do it.” He said: “He is right.” He said: “Then by the one who sent you, may God command you.” With this? He said: “Yes.” He said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not add anything to them nor take anything away from them.” Then when he left, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If he is truthful.” They will enter Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2385","I am Issa bin Hammad, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Sharik bin Abi Nimr, that he heard Anas bin Malik say: While we were sitting in The Mosque A man came on a camel, and he guided it in the mosque, then untangled it, and said to them: Which of you is Muhammad? And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was reclining between them. We said to him: This is the white man reclining. Then the man said to him: O son of Abdul-Muttalib, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “I have answered you,” and the man said: I am asking you, O Muhammad, and there is hardship for you in this matter. The question is, do not find it difficult for me to do so. So he said: “Ask whatever you wish.” The man said: “I called upon you by your Lord and by the Lord of those before you. God has sent you.” To all people? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” He said: So I adjure you by God, has God commanded you to pray the five daily prayers? And tonight? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” He said: So I adjure you by God, has God commanded you that we fast this month of the year? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” He said: I adjure you by God. God has commanded you to take this charity from Our rich and divide it among our poor? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” The man said: I believe in what you have brought, and I am a messenger from those of my people behind me, and I Dimam bin Tha'labah is a brother and Banu Sa'd bin Bakr. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2386","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim told us from his book, he said: My uncle told us, and he is Ya’qub bin Ibrahim. He said: Laith told us, he said: Tell me. Ibn Ajlan, and other of our brothers, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, that he heard Anas bin Malik, He says: While we were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting in the mosque, a man came in on a camel, and he leaned on it in the mosque, then he licked it, then He said: Which of you is Muhammad, and he was reclining between them, so we said to him: This is the white man reclining? The man said to him: O Ibn Abdul Muttalib, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have answered you.” The man said: O Muhammad, I He asked you and insisted on your question. He said: “Ask whatever you wish.” He said: I adjure you by your Lord and the Lord of those before you. God has sent you to the people. All of them? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” He said: So I adjure you by God, has God commanded you that we fast this month of the year? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” He said: I adjure you by God. God has commanded you to take this charity from our rich people. So you divide it among our poor? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By God, yes.” The man said: I believe in what you have brought, and I am a messenger from those of my people behind me, and I Dimam ibn Tha'labah is a brother of Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2387","Abu Bakr bin Ali told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Amara Hamza bin Al-Harith bin Umair told us, he said: I heard my father mentioning On the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was with his companions. A man from the desert came to them and said: Which of you is Ibn Abd al-Muttalib? They said: This is the bright ochre. Hamza said: The white ochre, tinged with red. He said: I am asking you and I will be difficult for you in the question. He said: “Ask whatever seems to you.” He said: I adjure you by the Lord of those before you and the Lord of those after you. Has God sent you? He said: “By God, yes.” He said: And I adjure you to do so. Has God commanded you to pray five prayers every day and night? He said: “By God, yes.” He said: And I adjure you by this, has God commanded you to take from the wealth of our rich and return it to our poor? He said: “By God, yes.” He said: And I adjure you to do so. Has God commanded you to fast this month out of the twelve months? He said: “By God, yes.” He said: And I adjure you to do so. Has God commanded you that we perform Hajj to this house, whoever is able to make a way to it? He said: “By God, yes.” He said: I believed and spoke the truth, and I am Dimam bin Tha’labah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2388","Suleiman bin Dawud reported, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utbah, that Abdullah bin Abbas used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the most generous of people, and he was the most generous of people. Ramadan when Gabriel met him, and Gabriel used to meet him every night of Ramadan and study the Qur’an with him. He said: To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted him when Gabriel met him, “More kind than the sent wind.”"
"2389","Muhammad bin Ismail told me, he said: Hafs bin Omar bin Al-Harith told me, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Muammar and Al-Nu’man told us. Ibn Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not curse a curse that can be mentioned, and it was If he is close to Gabriel, he studies him, he is more generous with goodness than the sent wind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2390","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail told us, Abu Suhail said: On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he said: “When the month of Ramadan begins, the gates of Paradise will be opened, the gates of Hell will be closed, and the devils will be chained up.”"
"2391","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub narrated, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Nafi’ bin Yazid narrated, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: Abu Suhail told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ramadan begins, the The gates of Paradise are closed, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained up.” Mention of the disagreement over Al-Zuhri regarding it."
"2392","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Nafi’ bin Abi Anas told me that his father told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If “Ramadan has come, the gates of Paradise have opened, the gates of Hell have been closed, and the devils have been chained.”"
"2393","Muhammad bin Khalid told us, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Abi Anas, a servant, told me Al-Taymiyyin, that his father told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ramadan comes, the The gates of mercy, the gates of hell are closed, and the devils are chained.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2394","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported in his hadith, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Abi Anas, that His father told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened.” And the gates of Hell were closed, and the devils were chained.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri."
"2395","Ubaid Allah bin Saad reported, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Anas, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “When the month of Ramadan begins, the gates of Paradise are opened and closed. Gates of Hell, and chains of devils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2396","Ubaid Allah bin Saad reported, he said: My uncle told me, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim mentioned, on the authority of Uwais bin Abi Uwais Adeid Bani Taim, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This Ramadan has come to you.” The gates of Paradise will be opened, the gates of Hell will be closed, and the devils will be chained therein.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is wrong. Ibn Ishaq did not hear it from Al-Zuhri, and what is correct is that we mentioned it before, mentioning the disagreement over Muammar in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2397","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, he said: Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri. On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wanted to perform Ramadan without any determination, and he said: “When he entered Ramadan, the gates of Paradise were opened, the gates of Hell were closed, and the devils were chained therein.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He was sent by Ibn The Blessed One (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2398","Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated, saying: Hibban ibn Musa al-Marwazi narrated, saying: Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When Ramadan begins, the gates of Paradise are opened, and the gates of Hell are closed. And the devils are chained.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2399","Bishr bin Hilal reported, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Ramadan has come to you, a blessed month in which God has made obligatory fasting upon you, in which the gates of heaven are opened and the gates of heaven are closed.” Hell, and the rebellious devils are chained therein. By God, therein is a night better than a thousand months. Whoever is deprived of its goodness has been deprived.”"
"2400","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Arfaja, he said: We returned Uqba ibn Farqad, So we remembered the month of Ramadan, and he said: What do you remember? We said: The month of Ramadan. He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “In it the gates of Paradise are opened, and the gates of Hell are closed.” And the devils are chained therein, and a caller calls out every night: O seeker of good, come, and O seeker of evil, desist.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Error (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2401","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Arfaja, he said: I was in A house in which was Utba bin Farqad. He said: I was narrating a hadith, and he was a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if he was more worthy of the hadith. The man spoke on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “In Ramadan, the gates of heaven are opened for him, the gates of Hell are closed, and he is chained up during it.” Every devil has a desire, and a caller calls out every night: O seeker of goodness, come, and O seeker of evil, desist.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And the hadith This section is more likely to be correct, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2402","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Muhallab told us. And Anba Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Al-Muhallab bin Abi Habiba, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Bakra, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Do not say: ‘None of you has fasted Ramadan, nor has it spent its entire night in prayer.’” I do not know whether he disliked purification or he said: There must be heedlessness and slumber. The wording is by Ubayd Allah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2403","Imran bin Yazid bin Khalid told me, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Ataa told me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas tells us, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a woman from the Ansar: “If it is Ramadan, perform Umrah therein, for Umrah Therein is a valid argument.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2404","Ali bin Hajar reported, he said: Ismail reported, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Abi Harmala, told us, he said: Kurayb informed me, that Umm Al-Fadl I sent him to Muawiyah in the Levant. He said: I came to the Levant and fulfilled her needs. The crescent of Ramadan began for me while I was in the Levant, and I saw The crescent was seen on Friday night, then I came to Medina at the end of the month, and Abdullah bin Abbas asked me, then he mentioned the crescent, and said: When did you see the crescent? I said: We saw him on Friday night. He said: Did you see him on Friday night? I said: Yes, and the people saw it and fasted, and Muawiyah fasted. He said: “But we saw it on the night of Saturday, so we will continue fasting until we complete thirty days or we see it. So I said: Isn’t it enough to see Muawiyah and his companions? He said: No, that’s what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2405","Musa bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He came A Bedouin went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I saw the crescent last night. He said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad His servant and Messenger? “I said: Yes. He said: “O Bilal, give the people the call to fast tomorrow.” Mention of the disagreement over Sufyan in the hadith of Simak. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2406","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz reported, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I saw the crescent. He said: “Do you bear witness that there is no god but God, and that Muhammad is His servant?” And His Messenger? He said: Yes. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for them to fast. Ahmad bin Sulayman reported, on the authority of Abu Dawud, on the authority of Sufyan, On the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, mursal. Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, in a mursal report. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2407","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Saeed bin Shabib Abu Uthman told me, and he was a righteous old man in Tarsus, he said: Ibn Abi informed me Zaida, on the authority of Hussein bin Al-Harith Al-Jadli, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Zayd bin Al-Khattab, that he addressed the people on the day in which there was doubt. He said: I sat with the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked them, and they told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “Fast at its sighting, break your fast at its sighting, and be silent for it. If it is cloudy for you, then complete thirty days, and if it is witnessed Two witnesses, then fast and break your fast.”"
"2408","I am Mu'mal bin Hisham, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Shu'bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “Fast when you see it, and break your fast when you see it. If the month is cloudy for you, then count thirty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2409","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: My father told us, he said: Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fast when the crescent is sighted and break your fast when it is sighted. If it is cloudy, then prepare Thirty “Mention of the disagreement over Al-Zuhri in this hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2410","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, he said: Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abraham told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. It is distressing for you, so fast for thirty days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2411","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman told me, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Salem bin Abdullah told me. On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If you see him, fast, and if you see him So break your fast, and if it is cloudy for you, prepare for it.”"
"2412","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin reported a reading from him, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned Ramadan and said: “Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not break your fast until You see it, but if it is difficult for you, then support it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2413","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Do not fast until you see it, and do not break your fast until you see it. If it is cloudy for you, prepare for it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2414","Abu Bakr bin Ali told me, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Ubaid told us By God, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned the crescent, and he said: “If you see it Then fast, and when you see it, break your fast, but if it is cloudy for you, then count thirty.” Mention of the disagreement over Amr bin Dinar in the hadith of Abdullah bin Abbas In it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2415","Ahmad bin Uthman told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fast for the crescent when it is sighted, and break the fast when it is sighted. If it is cloudy, complete the number of thirty.”"
"2416","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hunayn, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I am amazed at those who start the month, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you see the crescent, then fast, and when you see it, then break your fast. If it is cloudy for you, then complete the period of thirty.” The disagreement over Mansour was mentioned in a Rub’i hadith in which (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2417","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i bin Harash, on the authority of Hudhayfah bin Al-Yaman, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not advance the month until you see the crescent or complete the waiting period, then fast until you see the crescent or complete the waiting period.” The waiting period before that.”"
"2418","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i, on the authority of some of the companions of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not advance the month until you have completed the waiting period, or you have seen the crescent, then “Fast, and do not break your fast until you have completed the waiting period or sighted the crescent.” Posted by Al-Hajjaj ibn Artat (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2419","Muhammad bin Hatim narrated, he said: Hibban narrated, he said: Abdullah narrated, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Artat, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Quarterly, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you see the crescent, fast, and when you see it, break your fast. So complete thirty, complete Sha`ban as thirty, unless you see the crescent before that, then fast Ramadan for thirty, unless you see the crescent before that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2420","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Hatem bin Abi Saghira narrated to us, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, On the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn Abbas told us, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Fast to see it, and break your fast to see it.” Then if a cloud comes between you and it, continue and do not face the month facing it.”"
"2421","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Do not fast before Ramadan. Fast on its sighting, and break your fast on its sighting. If an absence prevents it, then complete it.” \"thirty\""
"2422","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr reported, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, who said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore that he would not have intercourse with his wives for a month, so he stayed for twenty-nine days, so I said: Haven’t you been alone for a month, so I counted The days are twenty-nine. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The month is twenty-nine.”"
"2423","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad reported, saying: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Abi Thawr told him. And Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Al-Hakam bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Shuaib told me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah told me Allah bin Abi Thawr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: I was still keen to ask Omar bin Al-Khattab about the two women from the wives of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, to whom God said: If you repent to God, then your hearts have been willing. The context of the hadith, in which he said: “So the Messenger of God retired May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his wives for the sake of that hadith, when Hafsa revealed it to Aisha twenty-nine nights. Aisha said: And he had said: “I will not stay with them for a month,” because of the severity of his feelings for them when God told him their story, and when twenty-nine had passed One night, he went to Aisha and started with her, and Aisha said to him: You had vowed, O Messenger of God, not to enter upon us for a month, and we We were counting twenty-nine nights in the morning, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The month has twenty-nine nights.” He mentioned the news. Ibn Abbas in it"
"2424","Amr ibn Yazid reported, on the authority of Bahz, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Gabriel came to me and said: The month has completed the twenty-nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2425","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Muhammad, and mentioned a word that means: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, he said: I heard Abu al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The month has twenty-nine days.” He mentioned the disagreement over Ismail in the story of Saad bin Malik in it (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2426","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr reported, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he struck one hand on the other, and said: “The month is like this, and such, and such.” And in the third, he subtracted “a finger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2427","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “The month is like this, and like this, and like this,” meaning: twenty-nine. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: It was narrated by Yahya bin Saeed and others, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Mursal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2428","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Saad bin Abi Waqqas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The month is like this, and like this, and like this,” and Muhammad bin Ubaid clapped his hands, followed by three claps. Then, in the third, he placed his thumb on the left. He mentioned the disagreement over Yahya bin Abi Kathir regarding the news of Abu Salamah, L4903, in it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2429","Abu Dawud narrated, he said: Harun narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The month may be twenty-nine or may be thirty, so when you see it, fast, and when you see it Then break your fast, and if it becomes cloudy for you, complete the number of thirty.”"
"2430","Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim told me. He said: I am Muhammad. He said: Muawiyah told us. And Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah told me, saying: Othman bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muawiyah, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, that Abu Salamah told him that he heard Abdullah, who was Ibn Umar, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The month is twenty-nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2431","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Qays, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Amr, on the authority of Ibn Umar On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “We are an illiterate nation. We do not write, nor do we count the month thus and so,” three times until he mentioned nine. And twenty (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2432","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, who said: I heard Saeed bin Amr Ibn Saeed Ibn Al-Aas, that he heard Ibn Omar, speaking on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “We are an illiterate nation, we do not count, nor do we write. And the month is like this, and like this, and like this,” and he held his thumb on the third, “and the month is like this and like this,” and like this, the completion of the thirtieth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2433","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Jablah ibn Suhaim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The month is like this,” and he described Shu’bah, on the authority of Jabalah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “that it is twenty-nine. As for what he narrated about his action, he did it twice with the fingers of his hands and shortened a finger on his third hand. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2434","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Uqba, he said: I heard Ibn Umar, saying: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The month is twenty-nine.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2435","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdul God, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have the suhoor meal, for there is a blessing in the suhoor meal.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ubaid Allah bin Happy (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2436","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdullah, “ “They had suhoor.” Ubayd Allah said: I don’t know how to pronounce it."
"2437","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Eat the suhoor meal, for there is a blessing in the suhoor meal.” The disagreement over Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman was mentioned in this hadith."
"2438","Ali bin Saeed bin Jarir narrated, saying: Abu Al-Rabi’ narrated to us, saying: Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat the suhoor meal, for there is a blessing in the suhoor meal.”"
"2439","Ahmad bin Suleiman reported, saying: Yazid told us, saying: Abd al-Malik reported, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said, “They had suhoor.” For there is a blessing in the suhoor.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Ibn Abi Laila rated it as a"
"2440","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Abi Laila told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Have the suhoor meal, for there is a blessing in the suhoor meal.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2441","Abdul-A'la bin Wasil bin Abdul-A'la reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Have the suhoor meal, for there is a blessing in the suhoor meal.”"
"2442","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Khallad told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, he said: Yahya bin Khallad told us Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Eat suhoor, for there is blessing in suhoor,” Abu Abdul Rahman: This hadith of Yahya bin Saeed, its chain of transmission is hasan, but it is objectionable, and I fear that the mistake is on the part of Muhammad bin Fudayl. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2443","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub reported, he said: Waki` reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, he said: We said to Hudhayfah: i.e. What time did you eat suhoor with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “It is daytime, but the sun has not risen.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2444","Muhammad ibn Bashar narrated, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Adi, he said: I heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: “I had suhoor with Hudhayfah, then we went out to pray, and when we came to the mosque, we prayed two rak’ahs, and the prayer was established, and there was only a moment between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2445","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Fudayl told me, he said: Abu Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibrahim told us, about his connection with Ibn Zufar. He said: “I had suhoor meal with Hudhayfah, then we went out to the mosque and prayed the two rak’ahs of dawn, then the prayer was established, and we prayed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2446","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Waki’ narrated, he said: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, he said: “We had dinner with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then we stood up for prayer. I said: How long was there between them? He said: It is as much as a man can recite fifty verses.” “It was mentioned that Hisham and Sa’id differed from Qatada in this hadith."
"2447","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, He said: “We had the suhoor meal with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then we stood up for prayer. I said: It is alleged that Anas said: What was in between that, he said: A man can recite fifty verses.”"
"2448","Abu Al-Ash’ath informed us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Zaid bin Thabit, then they got up and entered the morning prayer. We said to Anas: How long was the time between them finishing and entering the prayer? He said: The amount of what a person recites is fifty verses. Mentioning the disagreement over Sulaiman bin Mihran in the hadith of Aisha regarding delaying suhoor, and the difference in their wording."
"2449","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abu Atiya, he said: I said to Aisha: Among us are two men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them hastens breaking the fast and delays suhoor, and the other delays breaking the fast. And he hastens the suhoor. She said: “Which one of them hastens the breaking of the fast and delays the suhoor?” I said: Abdullah. She said: “This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was like.” May God’s peace and blessings be upon him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2450","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamah, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, he said: I said: To Aisha: Among us are two men from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them hastens the breaking of the fast and delays suhoor, and the other delays breaking the fast. And he hastens the suhoor. She said: “Which one of them hastens the breaking of the fast and delays the suhoor?” I said: Abdullah bin Masoud. She said: “This is what the Messenger of God was like.” May God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2451","Ahmad bin Suleiman reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Atiya, he said: I entered And Masruq was told to Aisha, and Masruq said to her: Two men from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, both of them do not turn away from goodness, one of them: He delays the prayer and breaking the fast, and the other: hastens the prayer and the breaking of the fast. Aisha said: “Which one of them hastens the prayer and the breaking of the fast?” Masruq said: Abdullah, Aisha said: “This is what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2452","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Atiya, who said: Masruq and I entered upon Aisha. So we said to her: O Mother of the Believers, there are two men from the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them hastens the breaking of the fast and the prayer, and the other delays the prayer. prayer and delays breaking the fast. She said: “Which one of them hastens breaking the fast and hastens the prayer?” We said: Abdullah bin Masoud. She said: “This is what he used to do.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” The other, Abu Musa (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2453","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abd al-Rahman reported, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid, the companion of al-Zayyadi, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith speaking, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. While he was enjoying himself, he said: “It is a blessing that God has given you, so do not neglect it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2454","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Yunus bin Saif, on the authority of Al Harith bin Ziyad, On the authority of Abu Rahm, on the authority of Al-Irbad bin Sariyah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, calling for suhoor during the month of Ramadan. He said: “Come to the blessed lunch.”"
"2455","Suwayd bin Nasr reported, he said: Abdullah reported, on the authority of Baqiya bin al-Walid, he said: Bujayr bin Saad told me, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma'dan, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Maadi Karab, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “You must eat the suhoor lunch, for it is the lunch \"The Blessed One\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2456","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: “Come to the blessed lunch,” meaning suhoor."
"2457","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Aas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The difference between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the one who eats pre-dawn prayers.”"
"2458","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said at dawn: “O Anas, I want to fast, feed me something.” So I brought him dates and a bowl of water. That was after Bilal gave the call to prayer, and he said: “O Anas, see a man eating with me.” So I called Zayd bin Thabit and he came and said: I drank a drink. Suwaiq, and I want to fast, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And I want to fast,” so he ate suhoor with him, then he got up and prayed two rak’ahs. Then he went out to pray"
"2459","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn bin Ayyash, a trustworthy and noble person from the people of Pajda told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us on the authority of Al-Baraa ibn Aazib, “If one of them slept before having dinner, it was not permissible for him to eat anything, nor He drinks his night and his day from tomorrow until the sun sets, until this verse was revealed: “And eat and drink” until the black thread. He said: It was revealed about Abu Qais bin Amr. He came to his family while he was fasting after sunset, and he said: Is there anything? Then his wife said: We don’t have anything Nothing, but I will go out and seek dinner for you. So I went out and he laid down his head and fell asleep. I returned to him and found him sleeping and woke him up and he did not eat anything. And he spent the night and fasting until the middle of the day, then he fainted. That was before this verse was revealed, so God revealed it.”"
"2460","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ash-Shabi, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, that he asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The white thread and the black thread are the blackness of the night and the whiteness of the day.”"
"2461","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, Bilal gives the call to prayer at night, so that your sleeper may wake up, and your leader may return, and it is not dawn for you to say thus,” and he gestured with his palm. But the dawn is when he says this and points with his two index fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2462","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah said, Sawadah bin Hanzalah reported, he said: I heard Samurah He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not be deceived by Bilal’s call to prayer or this whiteness until dawn breaks like this and like this.” Meaning, objecting. Abu Dawud said: So he spread out his hands to the right and to the left, extending his hands."
"2463","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not fast before the month, except for a man who used to fast and that day came after his fast. “It was mentioned that Yahya bin Abi Kathir and Muhammad bin Amr disagreed with Abu Salamah regarding it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2464","Imran bin Yazid bin Khalid told me, he said: Muhammad bin Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Awza’i informed, on the authority of Yahya, he said: he told me Abu Salamah said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should advance the month by one day or two days.” Except if someone is fasting, let him fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2465","Muhammad ibn al-Ala informed us, he said: Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do not precede the month by fasting one or two days, unless that coincides with a day on which one of you used to fast.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2466","Shuaib bin Yusuf and Muhammad bin Bashar narrated, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Abdul Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour. On the authority of Salem, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fast for two consecutive months, except... He used to connect Sha`ban with Ramadan.” The disagreement over Muhammad ibn Ibrahim was mentioned in this hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2467","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Anbari’s repentance, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, On the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to connect Sha`ban with Ramadan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2468","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman reported, saying: Ibn Hab told us, saying: Usama bin Zaid reported, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim told him, on the authority of Abu Salamah Bin Abdul Rahman, that he asked Aisha about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He fasts so much that we say he does not break his fast, and he breaks his fast so much so that we say he does not fast, and he used to fast during Sha’ban or all of Sha’ban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2469","Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Yazid told us, that Ibn Al-Hadi told him, that Muhammad bin Ibrahim narrated to him, on the authority of Abu Salamah, narrated to him, on the authority of Aisha, who said: One of us used to break the fast in Ramadan, so she was unable to do so. It is to be made up until Sha`ban begins, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would not fast in a month. He would not fast in Sha`ban. He used to fast its entirety except A little, but he used to fast it all of it.” Mention of the difference in wording of those reporting Aisha’s story about it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2470","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: Tell me about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “He used to fast so that we would say: He has fasted, and he would break his fast so that we would say: He said: He broke his fast, and he did not fast a month longer than Sha’ban. He used to fast only a little of Sha’ban. He used to fast all of Sha’ban. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2471","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Muadh bin Hisham reported, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not in more than one month of the year.” He fasted during Sha’ban, and he used to fast all of Sha’ban.”"
"2472","Ahmad bin Suleiman reported, saying: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast in Sha`ban. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2473","Harun bin Ishaq reported, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Sa`d bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I do not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the entire Qur’an in one night, nor did he stay in prayer for a night until the morning, nor did he fast for a month.” “Never in full, other than Ramadan.”"
"2474","Muhammad bin Ahmad told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, he said: I asked her about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to fast until we say He has fasted, and he breaks his fast, so much so that we say: He has broken his fast, and he has not fasted a full month since he came to Medina, unless it is Ramadan.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"2475","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled, who is Ibn Al-Harith, told us, on the authority of a whisper, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: I said To Aisha: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the Duha prayer? She said: “No, unless he comes from the place where he was gone.” I said: Was he fasting for an entire month? She said: “I have never known him to fast an entire month except Ramadan, and he would not break his fast until he had fasted from it, until he went on his way.”"
